Per-team scoring events matched on average but not in structure: with equal TD counts and a
one-FG difference the real margin is exactly 3 in 71% of games, the sim's in 45%.
D35: the two-point decision is near-deterministic by exact post-TD differential; the 7-bucket
table smeared it. Complete grid with measured-k shrinkage, loaded via _CACHE.
D36: u_pat decided the two-point question and then the XP make (biased ~92% in trailing Q4);
own uniforms now.
D37: test_dead_tables_5a5._run left its last override in the engine cache for every later
module — prior full-suite counts were contaminated; fixed, and the assert-True two-point
placeholder is a real test.
K1: P(|final|=3) 8.1 -> 10.6% (14.5); 3-composition exact 45 -> 61%. Clean suite 89 pass / 4 red.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
